  "details": "<p>GANE OBJECT 7437</p>\r\n<p>Bal\u0101w\u0101t is known for its famed \"bronze\" gates. These were likely bronze-strapped or studded wooden gates that were part of a ninth century B.C. palace of <span>Ashurbanipal II (884-859 BC) and his successor,\u00a0</span>Shalmaneser III (858-824 BC).</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Bal\u0101w\u0101t is the site of the ancient Assyrian city of Imgur-Enlil. A place from the TAVO Index.",
